# Authentik flows

## Gate

Use when the user asks about Authentik **flows**, **stages**, bindings,
enrollment, authentication, recovery, or invalidation flows. Skip
app/provider-only asks unless a flow pk must be resolved for binding.

## Transport

No Authentik MCP discovered. Use Authentik REST API with resolved base
URL + Bearer token (never echo the token). Prefer a real Authentik MCP
later without inventing tool names.

## Resolve ids

Never invent flow `pk`, `slug`, or stage UUIDs. Resolve via:

| Need | API |
| --- | --- |
| List flows | `GET /api/v3/flows/instances/` |
| Get flow | `GET /api/v3/flows/instances/{slug}/` |
| Search flows | `GET /api/v3/flows/instances/?search=TERM` |
| Stages (all) | `GET /api/v3/flows/stages/all/` |
| Bindings on flow | inspect flow detail / stage bindings endpoints the instance exposes |

Designations that matter for providers: authentication, authorization,
invalidation, enrollment, recovery, unenrollment — report the
`designation` field when present.

## Receipt shape

Report: **name**, **slug**, **designation**, stage count / stage class
names when useful. Do not dump stage configuration secrets (SMTP
passwords, webhook tokens, CAPTCHA keys).

## Craft (gated)

Create / reorder / rebind stages need an **explicit verb** naming the
flow (or create intent). Prefer cloning a known-good flow over building
a blank enrollment chain from scratch unless the user asked for that.

| Action | API shape |
| --- | --- |
| Create flow | `POST /api/v3/flows/instances/` |
| Patch flow | `PATCH /api/v3/flows/instances/{slug}/` |
| Stage bindings | use the instance’s stage-binding endpoints after listing stages |

When attaching a flow to a provider, pass the resolved flow pk into
`authentik-providers` — do not leave providers on default flows unless
the user asked for defaults.

## MFA / recovery / enrollment risk

Changes that **weaken** MFA, skip identification, open public enrollment,
or alter recovery/unenrollment are high risk. Require:

1. Explicit verb this turn naming the **flow slug**.
2. One-sentence risk (what control is removed).
3. `authentik-safety` compliance.

Bare “simplify login” / “fix SSO” without naming the flow is **not**
authorization to drop MFA stages.

## Defaults

1. Read-only list/get is the default.
2. Prefer listing existing flows before creating parallel ones with
   similar names.
3. Cap stage dumps — summarize class names; open one stage detail when
   debugging a named failure.
4. Branding / CSS themes are out of scope unless the user named a flow
   presentation change.

## Symptom hints

| Signal | Likely check |
| --- | --- |
| Redirect loop after login | authorization vs authentication flow on the provider |
| MFA not prompted | identification / authenticator validation stages on the auth flow |
| Cannot enroll | enrollment flow designation + invitation/policy bindings |
| Logout leaves session | invalidation flow bound on the provider |

## Refuse

- Inventing flow slugs or stage UUIDs.
- Weakening MFA/recovery without an explicit named-flow verb.
- Pasting SMTP / webhook / CAPTCHA secrets from stage config into chat.
